; The one process harness for test/ppx. Every fixture directory here
; asks the same question of a real generated runner — what does it print,
; what does it exit with — and diffs the answer against a committed
; golden, so every directory needs the same two things: an environment
; scrubbed of anything a developer's shell could carry into the
; transcript, and a mask over the numbers that are measured rather than
; computed. Drive_harness holds both; drive.exe turns a directory's rule
; into runs. What a fixture pins now reads in its own rule.
;
; test/conformance drives its corpus through its own drive.exe: that one
; also materializes placeholder .corrected files, which is a corpus
; concern, not a transcript one.

(library
 (name drive_harness)
 (modules drive_harness)
 (libraries unix))

(executable
 (name drive)
 (modules drive)
 (libraries drive_harness unix))
